
<main>
<header class="top">
  <div class="eyebrow">PDE-RSI · results as of 21 October 2026</div>
  <h1>PDE-RSI Benchmark Results</h1>
  <p class="lede">Each agent identifies an unknown PDE from 256 noisy samples and writes a solver. This page compares a single model request, your RSI harness (v1 and v2), and the native coding agents (Claude Code with Opus 5.5, Codex with GPT-5.5). Every model runs with the same task, evaluator, sandbox and budget. The second half lists every benchmark equation, split and setting.</p>
  <nav class="toc" aria-label="Sections">
    <a href="#headline">Headline: fresh hidden splits</a><a href="#fresh-pde">Per PDE: fresh splits</a>
    <a href="#single">Inventory single runs</a><a href="#earlier">Earlier sealed splits</a>
    <a href="#other">Benchmarks without a native agent</a><a href="#tex">tex suite equations</a>
    <a href="#inventory">Inventory equations</a><a href="#manufactured">Manufactured suites</a><a href="#settings">Settings</a>
  </nav>
  <div class="defs">
    <div class="def"><b>Single run</b><span>One model request with the task, contract and starting diagnostics. The returned solver is frozen as is: no feedback, retry or gate.</span></div>
    <div class="def"><b>Single + repair</b><span>A single run that may fix one rule violation. If its one answer is rejected before running (code rules, program length) or cut off, that rejection is sent back once and one corrected answer is accepted. No solver runs before the repair.</span></div>
    <div class="def"><b>RSI · v1 / v2</b><span>Gated rounds whose accepted candidates pass on their workflow and memory. v2 adds modular programs with patch edits, a per-part gate, and run-time self-check guidance.</span></div>
    <div class="def"><b>Native agent</b><span>Claude Code or Codex in a sandbox with the same evaluator. Unlimited training runs, at most 30 gated validation submissions.</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="headline">
  <h2>Headline: fresh hidden splits</h2>
  <p>These splits were created on 20 October, after the earlier sealed splits had been used to diagnose the harness. No configuration saw them. Each cell shows the mean cases passed per run over 3 runs, then the per-run results and the development cost per run.</p>
  {{FRESH_SUMMARY_TEX}}
  {{FRESH_SUMMARY_INV}}
  <ul class="findings">
    <li><b>Opus 5.5:</b> RSI v2 passes every hidden case in all six runs (20/20 and 12/12) and ties Claude Code on both suites. With one rule repair, the single run reaches 9.0 (v1) and 10.7 (v2) of 12 on the inventory suite, against 0 without it.</li>
    <li><b>GPT-5.5:</b> RSI v2 improves on v1 on the tex suite (11.0 against 9.7) and costs less on both suites. It is still slightly behind Codex: 11.0 against 12.0 and 9.0 against 9.7. With three runs per configuration, these gaps are within the run-to-run spread.</li>
    <li><b>The repair changes only the Opus inventory single runs.</b> All 18 other single runs had a valid first answer, so their strict and repaired results are the same.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

